    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for June 30 is headlined by **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38), both of whom capitalize on a prime matchup against Fedde. The +19% boost from Fedde\u2019s projected struggles, combined with an aggressive park factor, makes this duo our primary engine for Runs and RBI. **Bryson Stott** (65.58) and **Luis Arraez** (64.99) round out the elite tier; **Bryson Stott** benefits significantly from a favorable platoon advantage against Chandler, while **Luis Arraez** remains a staple at the top of the order, leveraging a 10% lineup position boost to maximize efficiency. We are also tracking the stolen base potential against Pfaadt, where **Jung Hoo Lee** (61.83), **Matt Chapman** (61.64), and **Drew Gilbert** (50.94) all receive a tactical \"Slow SP Delivery\" bump, which is critical given our focus on the scarcity of SB in this format.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision of the day was **Daulton Varsho** (49.53), who sat just outside our active threshold. While **Daulton Varsho** projects well against RHP, the matchup against McLean (3.28 xERA) suppressed his ceiling, making him a less efficient option than our locked-in starters who benefit from softer SP profiles. We continue to monitor the status of **Will Smith** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** on the IL, as their absence remains the largest drag on our aggregate scoring capacity. Conversely, **Cal Raleigh** (53.51) barely holds onto his spot; his score is hampered by a negative park factor and a dynamic platoon disadvantage, but he remains in the fold to provide stability at the C1 position. Owners should keep a close eye on weather reports across the board, but currently, the primary risk is the volatility of the Pfaadt matchup, which dictates the performance variance for a large portion of our active roster.",
